## The four services

### 1. Cloudflare — DNS only
- Owns DNS for `curbsidescore.com`.
- Not used for CDN/proxy/security features — everything is set to "DNS only" on purpose, because Vercel and Railway need to see direct traffic to manage SSL themselves.
- Also hosts DNS records Resend needs for email sending (SPF/DKIM/MX — the `send.`, `resend._domainkey`, and `_railway-verify` type records).

### 2. Vercel — one project under the `curbside1` team
- **`curbside-app`** — Next.js app serving everything: landing page, pricing, sign-in, saved evaluations, account. Domains: `curbsidescore.com`, `www.curbsidescore.com`, `app.curbsidescore.com`. Calls the Railway backend via API — holds no data itself.
- **`curbsideprod`** (dashboard name `usecurbside`) — the old static landing page. To be retired once the apex is moved; Vercel will not attach a domain to two projects, so remove it there before adding it to `curbside-app`.
- They were deliberately separate while the landing page was static and the app was one private page. Merging them is what makes a shared header, one sign-in state and a pricing → account path possible at all.
- Env var on the project: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.curbsidescore.com`.

### 3. Railway — the backend
- Runs the FastAPI backend (Postgres + API), reachable at `api.curbsidescore.com`.
- Reads `$PORT` dynamically at runtime (not hardcoded).
- Runs `alembic upgrade head` automatically on every deploy/boot — schema migrations apply themselves.
- Environment variables that matter here:
  - `DEAL_RATER_CORS_ORIGINS` — must include `https://curbsidescore.com` or the website's API calls fail with CORS errors. Keep `https://app.curbsidescore.com` in the list too: a magic link opened at `app.` redirects to the apex, but nothing is lost by leaving it and something breaks if it is removed early.
  - `DEAL_RATER_APP_BASE_URL` — `https://curbsidescore.com` now. This is what builds the link in the sign-in email; leaving it on `app.` still works via the redirect, but every new email would take a needless hop.
  - `DEAL_RATER_SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN` — set to `.curbsidescore.com` so the auth cookie works across the `app.` subdomain.
  - `DEAL_RATER_RESEND_API_KEY` — required for magic-link sign-in emails to send; without it, sign-in returns 503.

### 4. Resend — transactional email
- Sends the magic-link sign-in emails for the website.
- Domain `curbsidescore.com` verified there via DNS records (added in Cloudflare).
- Requires: verified domain status + a valid API key in Railway's env vars + the "from" address in the backend code matching the verified domain. A 403 from Resend usually means one of those three is off.

