## Key gotchas worth remembering

- **DNS-only, not proxied** — Cloudflare's proxy (orange cloud) breaks Vercel's and Railway's own SSL cert issuance. Every record for this project should stay grey cloud.
- **All three web hostnames must live on the `curbside-app` Vercel project's Domains settings.** The apex and `www` start out on the old landing-page project and have to be removed there first — Vercel refuses to attach one domain to two projects, and the error does not say which other project is holding it.
- **Stale DNS caches (local machine, router, or browser) can make a correctly-configured domain look broken** even when the DNS record itself is fine. Test on a different network (e.g. phone hotspot) before assuming a config problem.
- **CORS origins must be an exact list, not `*`**, because the backend uses credentialed requests (cookies) — Starlette will break `*` + credentials combinations.
- **Extension `host_permissions` changes require a new Chrome Web Store version.** Existing installs stay on the old backend URL until that update is published and auto-updates on the user's machine.